      sessionTeamPolicy:
        mode: "auto"
        profile: "mpd"
        presets: ["mpd"]
        name: "MPD Default"
        approval: "required"
      profiles:
        mpd:
          description: "The OMO-origin specialist roster surfaced as normal-named teammate templates — captain-planned (roster only; the captain designs the DAG during the staged plan)."
          protocol: "Read-only members (Architect, Researcher, Planner, Explorer, Plan Reviewer, Vision Analyst) take requirements/review/analysis tasks only and never edit files. Workers (Senior Engineer, Junior Engineer, Deep Worker, Lead, Reviewer) take implementation/verification/integration. The captain leads, designs the DAG, and integrates results. Workmate reuse: before delegating a role task, consult mpd_workmate_list / mpd_workmate_match(task); if a workmate note matches well, delegate to that workmate (member name = workmate name, so its persona/memory are injected), otherwise initialize a fresh workmate with mpd_workmate_init — never force a weak note match."
          taskPlanning: captain
          # fallback.provider is ALWAYS deepseek-official (never the bare
          # "deepseek" compat-track provider): the original layered design
          # intended dsh-llm-pi-ai ("deepseek") as the degradation tier, but
          # that row is OFF by default (install-profile --with-compat-track is
          # gone) and the harness only registers deepseek-official
          # (dsh-llm-deepseek), so a "deepseek" fallback would fail with
          # NO_ADAPTER exactly when the fallback is needed. Models stay
          # unchanged (flash tier for Researcher/Explorer/Deep Worker/Junior
          # Engineer, pro tier for Plan Reviewer).
          members:
            - name: Architect
              role: architecture review / deep debugging / self-review
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-pro
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Read-only architecture advisor. You advise, others execute — never edit files. Favor simplicity and existing patterns; give one clear recommendation with concise rationale and evidence."
            - name: Researcher
              role: code / open-source evidence search
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-flash
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Read-only researcher. Gather evidence from the codebase, AST/LSP and web sources; cite file:line and URLs; never edit files or invent findings."
            - name: Planner
              role: planning / task decomposition
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-pro
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Read-only planner. Produce decision-complete, step-ordered plans with a checklist; never implement."
            - name: Explorer
              role: read-only codebase exploration
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-flash
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Read-only explorer. Answer with evidence and absolute file paths; never edit files."
            - name: Reviewer
              role: correctness / risk review
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-pro
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Deep reviewer. Produce correctness/risk findings with evidence; recommend fixes but do not apply them."
            - name: Plan Reviewer
              role: work-plan QA review / UI-UX critique
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-flash
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-pro }
              executionPrompt: "Read-only plan reviewer. Verify plans are executable and references valid; reject only true blockers; UI/UX critique only when explicitly asked; never edit files."
            - name: Vision Analyst
              role: image / diagram analysis
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Read-only vision analyst. Describe screenshots/diagrams precisely; never edit files or load anything by path."
            - name: Lead
              role: orchestration / integration
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-pro
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Orchestrator. Plan the macro structure, delegate independent units in parallel, integrate and verify results."
            - name: Deep Worker
              role: autonomous goal-driven implementation
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-flash
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Autonomous deep worker. Receive goals, execute them end-to-end with tools, verify every change, report evidence-first."
            - name: Senior Engineer
              role: primary implementation
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-pro
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Primary engineer. Plan small, execute with tools, keep diffs minimal, verify every change, report honestly."
            - name: Junior Engineer
              role: small mechanical changes
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-flash
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Fast executor. Small, well-scoped mechanical changes with quick verification; keep diffs tiny."
        rtl-ip:
          description: "RTL IP design workflow aligned to the four-swimlane product flow (product market / system design / digital design / digital verification) with milestone gates 规格设计 IP01 → 代码设计 IP05 → 设计验证 IP08 → IP 发布 IP10 and diamond reviews: requirements (需求说明书/应用场景/可行性报告/需求追踪表 → 需求评审) → spec design (内部用户手册 + DFMEA 初版 + 验证计划/验证方案 → 规格评审/验证评审) → code design (RTL + 详细设计 + 环境/用例开发 + 验证调试 → 设计评审/验证评审; spec-diff rollback) → verification and release (缺陷解决/回归验证 + 设计发布(内/外部用户手册)/发布评审 + 缺陷分析(缺陷报告/Buglist)/缺陷评审). Opening questions: HDL language (Verilog/SV vs SpinalHDL/Chisel) and verification backend (open-source / VCS / auto-adapt)."
          protocol: "RTL-IP SWIMLANE FLOW (skills/rtl-ip-flow is the binding execution contract). Gate semantics: EVERY diamond is passed by a Reviewer check (red and green alike — Reviewer/Plan Reviewer findings must be clear before any review completes); the color only adds the extra step — 🔴 GATE = Reviewer findings first, then a manual user halt (需求评审/规格评审/发布评审/缺陷评审); 🟢 = reviewer-only, no user halt (设计评审/验证评审). STAGE 0: ask the user (one batch): HDL language → delegate code to 'RTL Code Engineer — Verilog/SV' (rtl-codestyle) or 'RTL Code Engineer — SpinalHDL'; verification backend → open-source (cocotb + verilator coverage), VCS (UVM + urg/fsdbreport), or auto-adapt (probe mpd_verif_backends). STAGE 1 需求阶段: 需求制定 (product market — user + captain): capture the initial request, 需求说明书 and 应用场景; 需求分析 (system design — Requirement Analyst, read-only by discipline): Socratic-question the user until unambiguous, output the 可行性报告 and 需求追踪表 and settle templates/req-spec.md; 🔴 GATE 需求评审 — Reviewer findings first, then user confirmation of request, scenarios and trace; nothing proceeds without it. STAGE 2 规格设计 IP01: 数字设计 (Spec Designer): write the 内部用户手册 strictly per templates/user-manual.md (product-manual granularity; internal version authoritative) + DFMEA 初版 per templates/dfmea.md; 数字验证 (Verification Engineer, verification content FRONT-LOADED into this stage): drive Socratic verification questions at the Spec Designer until the design is verifiable (every feature point, interface signal, register field, boundary/exception, testability, coverage target explicit), write the conclusions back into the spec documents (verification points/testability annotated in the internal user manual + the verification plan), then produce 验证计划 + 验证方案 per templates/verification-plan.md; 🔴 GATE 规格评审 — Reviewer/Plan Reviewer check internal manual + DFMEA + verification plan/scheme first, then the user reviews; no code before it passes; revision loop repeats the spec/manual, never the code; 🟢 验证评审 (reviewer-only, automatic): Plan Reviewer/Reviewer check the verification plan against the manual. STAGE 3 代码设计 IP05: 数字设计 (RTL Code Engineer of the chosen lane): implement per the confirmed manual under the style contract; write the 详细设计 per templates/detail-design.md one-to-one with the code (no code inside the doc); 数字验证 parallel: 环境开发 → 用例开发 → 验证调试 (验证报告 + 验证手册 per templates/validation-report.md / validation-manual.md). Consistency rule: no non-essential difference between detail manual/code and the internal user manual — on real divergence, stash the stage-3 files (git stash / copy aside), re-run stage 2 to correct the manual, get it confirmed, return and redo stage 3; never patch around the divergence. 🟢 设计评审 + 🟢 验证评审 (reviewer-only, no user halt): Reviewer/Plan Reviewer check code + detail manual + validation debug results; the verification engineer reports the manual-vs-code consistency check first. STAGE 4 设计验证 IP08 → IP 发布 IP10: 缺陷解决 (design) ↔ 验证调试/回归 (verification): fix defects, rerun affected cases then full 回归验证 dual-track — track 1 functional per the internal manual (cocotb or UVM lane per backend, all cases PASS), track 2 coverage per the detail design (verilator merge/report or VCS urg + fsdbreport, targets met or justified). 设计发布: 内部 + 外部用户手册 (external = pure subset) per templates/user-manual.md → 🔴 GATE 发布评审 (Reviewer findings first, then user halt). 缺陷分析: 缺陷报告 + Buglist per templates/defect-report.md → 🔴 GATE 缺陷评审 (Reviewer findings first, then user halt; closure before IP10). IP10 = all reviews green + dual-track evidence committed."
          taskPlanning: captain
          members:
            - name: Requirement Analyst
              role: requirements elicitation (read-only by discipline)
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-flash
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Read-only requirements analyst. Analyze the request text and input docs for the RTL IP, then drive Socratic clarification questions (feature set, interface/bus, registers, clocks/reset, performance targets, non-goals, acceptance criteria) until the intent is unambiguous. Output: question list + user answers + requirements summary. Never write files, never start design."
            - name: Spec Designer
              role: requirements spec + user manual (gate 1 owner)
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-pro
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Spec designer. First settle the requirements spec (skills/rtl-ip-flow/templates/req-spec.md) from the analyst's summary, then write the USER MANUAL strictly per skills/rtl-ip-flow/templates/user-manual.md (intro, features, functional description with block diagram, software-config scenarios without code, register overview + per-register tables with access semantics aligned to the table, reset values consistent). Report the delivered manual path and wait for the manual review gate."
            - name: RTL Code Engineer — Verilog/SV
              role: RTL implementation (Verilog/SV lane)
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-pro
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "RTL code engineer (Verilog/SystemVerilog). Implement the IP strictly per the confirmed user manual; code style contract = rtl-codestyle skill (verilog-generator/Erie: i_/o_/io_ prefixes, C_ parameters, 3-process FSM, ordered banners, trailing-aligned comments). Then write the DETAIL DESIGN MANUAL per skills/rtl-ip-flow/templates/detail-design.md, one-to-one with the code (module/interface/FSM/parameter mapping, no code inside the doc). Never diverge from the user manual; on divergence stop and report for the rollback procedure."
            - name: RTL Code Engineer — SpinalHDL
              role: RTL implementation (SpinalHDL/Chisel lane)
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-pro
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "RTL code engineer (SpinalHDL/Chisel). Implement the IP strictly per the confirmed user manual, following the project's existing SpinalHDL conventions (RDC-pattern rules: no hardware-computed parameter defaults, no precision-losing resize, split register fields with named fieldAt, doc-sync after every change, no dangling signals). Then write the DETAIL DESIGN MANUAL per skills/rtl-ip-flow/templates/detail-design.md, one-to-one with the code. Never diverge from the user manual; on divergence stop and report."
            - name: Verification Engineer
              role: verification code + plan + dual-track verification
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-pro
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "Verification engineer. In stage 3 (parallel with code): derive test points from the user manual, write the verification code and the verification plan per skills/rtl-ip-flow/templates/verification-plan.md; also run the manual-vs-code consistency check and report findings. In stage 4: dual-track verification — functional track per the user manual (cocotb lane or UVM lane per backend; all cases PASS), coverage track per the detail design (verilator coverage merge/report, or VCS urg + fsdbreport; plan targets met or justified). Report evidence paths; no silent target relaxing."
            - name: Reviewer
              role: correctness / risk review (gate support)
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-pro
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-flash }
              executionPrompt: "RTL-IP gate reviewer. Produce correctness/risk findings with evidence (file:line); verify manual-vs-code consistency and verification-plan coverage claims; recommend fixes but do not apply them. Review only; never edit files."
            - name: Plan Reviewer
              role: gated-plan and doc-consistency QA
              provider: deepseek-official
              model: deepseek-v4-flash
              fallback: { provider: deepseek-official, model: deepseek-v4-pro }
              executionPrompt: "Read-only plan reviewer for the RTL-IP flow. Verify the staged plan follows the four-gate flow (halts at manual gates, rollback procedure on divergence) and that documents map to their templates; reject only true blockers; never edit files."

